Z||000010||Oreif||12-29-2000||12:24 AM||||HAHA that is funny! Does the interior orange paint add HP too! With all the porting and the large exhaust bet it's a real dog for torque. He also states the chassis has 193,000 miles on it. That's 66.6 miles per day, every day, for 8 years. I also have a hard time believing anyone would spend the kind of money he's talking about into the head of a 68,000 mile motor and not do anything to the lower end. Sounds like the car has been beat upon. Over 100 "Import" Decals? I thought ACCEL was made in the USA?||||reg||10
Z||000011||LZeitgeist||12-30-2000||09:58 AM||||Also quoted from the ad:<BR>"Here are some of the things on the engine there's many more just don't have enough space to write..."<P>The bid is, amazingly enough, up to $12,100...<P>I have to say, that's the riciest POS I've ever laid eyes on... and since when does eBay only give you so much space to write a description? What he meant to say was "There's other stuff too - honest - but I'm too lazy to go look at my car and make up more stuff to write in the ad."<P>Yeah, to each their own, but the worst thing about these vomit-inducing roving eyesores is coming to the realization that all that stuff was done voluntarily by the owner of the thing... damn, I've seen vandals screw up a car less effectively than some of the stuff going on these days under the guise of 'customization'. I can't wait to translate 'Fiero' into Japanese kanji and stick it diagonally across my hood, and let's find the Chinese word for 'Formula' and stick those on my doors, too...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>When I see a Fiero with the wheels spaced out of the wheelwells like one of these riceboy rollerskates, I'm gonna rip off all my clothes and run screaming into the night...<p>[This message has been edited by LZeitgeist (edited 12-30-2000).]||||reg||1
